# 30-Car Championship Cups

> Scope: extending the existing 30-car race support from Single Race to
> championship cups, including cup opponent persistence, race setup, result
> display, points storage, and UI/generator limits.

## Goal

Championship cups should support up to 30 total cars: the player plus up to 29
CPU opponents.

The cup should generate its CPU opponent roster once at cup start and keep that
same roster for every stage in the cup. The roster is driven by the cup's
`NumCars` value and class distribution fields:

- `NumCars`: total cars in the cup, including the player.
- `Classes`: per-rating CPU counts, currently represented in the DLL as
  `maxRookie`, `maxAmateur`, `maxAdvanced`, `maxSemiPro`, `maxPro`, and
  `maxSuperPro`.
- The sum of the six class counts must equal `NumCars - 1`.

Each cup race that has more than 16 cars still needs the existing 30-car race
fixes:

- participant expansion to the target count,
- stable CPU model selection,
- corrected 30-car grid placement,
- player back-of-grid placement after native ranking exists,
- post-race leaderboard rendering through the Clockwork Carnage table.

Championship standings must also support more than 16 cars:

- the `Points` table needs entries for positions 1 through 30,
- standings/total points storage must not truncate after 16 cars,
- the championship points table display needs a compact style similar to the
  Clockwork Carnage result table when car count is above 16.

## Current State

The repo already has a partial 30-car runtime path for Single Race.

Relevant existing behavior:

- `DLL/Mods/30CarMod.cpp` has the main 30-car helpers:
  - `GetTargetRaceCarCount` clamps against `randomizerMaxCarCount`.
  - `CacheRandomModels` builds the model list currently used by expanded races.
  - `ExpandRaceParticipantsToThirty` adds participant records.
  - `ApplyThirtyCarGrid` lays out a 5 by 6 grid.
  - `MovePlayersToBackAfterRacePositions` moves the player after ranking exists.
  - `ResetThirtyCarModState` clears per-race state.
- `DLL/Mods/30CarMod.cpp:189` currently limits support to
  `MODE_SINGLE_RACE`. Championship mode is `MODE_CHAMPIONSHIP` in
  `DLL/Game/RVGLStructs.h:102`.
- `DLL/Mods/RaceInitHooks.cpp` wires the race lifecycle:
  - `Hook_RaceSessionSetup` resets 30-car state.
  - `Hook_AssignStartPositions` expands participants before native start
    assignment.
  - `Hook_SetupAllRaceCars` applies the custom grid after native setup.
  - `Hook_UpdateRacePositions` applies the player back-of-grid swap.
  - `Hook_DrawPostRaceLeaderboard` temporarily changes the game mode to
    `MODE_CLOCKWORK_CARNAGE` when `participantCount > 16`.
- `DLL/Mods/RandomizerState.h:16` defines `randomizerMaxCarCount = 30`.
- `DLL/Mods/RandomizerState.h:47` defines `ThirtyCarRuntimeState`, and
  `DLL/Mods/RandomizerState.h:86` stores it inside the global randomizer
  context.

The current cup profile mirror is still 16-position oriented:

- `DLL/Game/RVGLStructs.h:139` defines `CupProfile`.
- `CupProfile::stages[16]` is at `DLL/Game/RVGLStructs.h:159`.
- `CupProfile::pointsTable[16]` is at `DLL/Game/RVGLStructs.h:162`.
- The struct size is asserted as `0x198`, so the native profile layout should
  not be expanded in place unless Ghidra proves there is unused room or another
  backing table exists.
- `DLL/Mods/CupHooks.cpp:114` already writes `cupConfig.numCars`.
- `DLL/Mods/CupHooks.cpp:120` writes the six class count fields.
- `DLL/Mods/CupHooks.cpp:129` only accepts points tables with at least 16
  entries, and `DLL/Mods/CupHooks.cpp:131` copies only 16 entries.

The generator/UI still enforce or emit 16-entry cup points data:

- `ui/src-tauri/src/randomizer/cups.rs:62` has `pad_points`, which truncates
  to 16 and pads to 16.
- `ui/src-tauri/src/randomizer/cups.rs:636` and `:662` emit padded cup points.
- `ui/src-tauri/src/randomizer/models.rs:481` defines the default 16-entry
  points table.
- `ui/src/configure/cupSpec/CupSpecTab.jsx:162` caps global cup car count at
  16.
- `ui/src/configure/cupSpec/CupConfigPage.jsx:294` caps per-cup car count at
  16.
- `ui/src/configure/cupSpec/CupUtils.jsx:222` limits active points to
  `Math.min(numCars, 16)`.
- `ui/src/configure/cupSpec/CupUtils.jsx:227` renders exactly 16 points inputs.

## Existing RVAs / Ghidra Locations

RVGL image base is `0x00400000`, so Ghidra virtual address is usually
`0x00400000 + RVA`.

| Purpose | RVA | Ghidra VA | Current code |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| Load default cups | `0x0004bae0` | `0x0044bae0` | `RVA_LOAD_VANILLA_CUPS` |
| Validate/check cup unlock | `0x00048840` | `0x00448840` | `RVA_CUP_VALIDATE_AND_CHECK_UNLOCK` |
| Cup stage finished | `0x0004b800` | `0x0044b800` | `RVA_CUP_ON_STAGE_FINISHED` |
| Draw post-race leaderboard | `0x00061370` | `0x00461370` | `RVA_DRAW_POST_RACE_LEADERBOARD` |
| Race session setup | `0x00050700` | `0x00450700` | `RVA_RACE_SESSION_SETUP` |
| Setup all race cars | `0x0004f7b0` | `0x0044f7b0` | `RVA_SETUP_ALL_RACE_CARS` |
| Assign start positions | `0x0004f980` | `0x0044f980` | `RVA_ASSIGN_START_POSITIONS` |
| Add participant and count | `0x0004f1f0` | `0x0044f1f0` | `RVA_ADD_PARTICIPANT_AND_COUNT` |
| Update race positions | `0x000075f0` | `0x004075f0` | `RVA_UPDATE_RACE_POSITIONS` |
| Game mode global | `0x002e34c0` | `0x006e34c0` | `RVA_GAME_MODE` |
| Current race participant count | `0x00b3eb04` | `0x00f3eb04` | `RVA_RACE_PARTICIPANT_COUNT` |
| Participant records | `0x00b3eb50` | `0x00f3eb50` | `RVA_RACE_PARTICIPANT_RECORDS` |
| Runtime `NCars` global | `0x00b43488` | `0x00f43488` | `RVA_NCARS` |
| Settings `NCars` global | `0x0aa8e930` | `0x0ae8e930` | `RVA_SETTINGS_NCARS` |

## Runtime Design Notes

Single Race currently derives extra CPU models from the player's car rating in
`PickRandomModel`. Championship cups need a different model source:

1. At cup start, resolve the active `CupProfile` and target `RandomizedCup`.
2. Read `NumCars` and the six class counts.
3. Build exactly `NumCars - 1` CPU model IDs from CPU-selectable cars, honoring
   each class count.
4. Persist that ordered model list for the whole cup.
5. For each cup stage, rebuild participant records from the persisted list
   rather than rolling new opponents.

The state should likely live outside the per-race-only reset path. A possible
shape is a new `ChampionshipThirtyCarState` in `RandomizerState.h`, containing:

- active cup ID or difficulty,
- target car count,
- generated CPU model IDs,
- per-stage runtime car IDs,
- points/standings cache if native storage cannot hold all positions.

`ResetThirtyCarModState` should continue to clear per-race values, but it should
not discard the cup roster while the same championship is active.

## Points And Standings

There are two separate problems:

1. Race results need a point value for positions 17 through 30.
2. Championship standings need to store and display totals for positions 17
   through 30.

Do not assume that `CupProfile::pointsTable[16]` can be changed to 30 in
`RVGLStructs.h`. The next known fields are `isUnlocked`, `isCHTModified`, and
padding, and the asserted native size is `0x198`.

Likely approaches to investigate:

- Leave native `CupProfile::pointsTable[16]` intact and intercept the function
  that reads position-to-points values. Return custom points for positions above
  16 from randomizer-managed storage.
- Leave native standings storage intact for 1 through 16 and maintain a
  randomizer-managed standings table for extra CPU cars.
- If native code has separate dynamic championship standings arrays, find their
  allocation and size checks, then patch the limits to 30.

The display path should be separate from storage. If the native championship
standings UI is fixed to 16 rows, hook the draw function and render a compact
30-car table using the same rendering primitives already used elsewhere:

- `RVA_DRAW_UI_TEXT`
- `RVA_DRAW_SPRITE_2D`
- `RVA_UI_DRAW_ROUNDED_RECT`
- `RVA_SETUP_GL_RENDER_STATE`
- `RVA_FLUSH_DEFERRED_UI_BATCHES`

## Ghidra Questions To Resolve

Before implementing, use Ghidra MCP to answer these:

1. Where is the championship cup initialized when the player starts a cup?
   We need the earliest stable hook point to generate the persistent CPU roster.
2. Which function reads `CupProfile::numCars` and class limits to choose cup
   CPU opponents?
3. Does RVGL already persist a cup opponent list across stages? If yes, find the
   storage address, element type, and reset lifetime.
4. Where are championship race participants copied into
   `RVA_RACE_PARTICIPANT_RECORDS`?
5. Where is `CupProfile::pointsTable[position]` read, and what happens for
   positions above 15?
6. Where are per-car championship total points stored? Determine whether the
   native storage is fixed at 16, tied to `NumCars`, or dynamically allocated.
7. Which function draws the championship standings/points table between races
   and at cup end?
8. Can the Clockwork Carnage display path be reused directly for cup race
   results, or does championship mode restore/overwrite state afterward?
9. What are the cup restart, abandon, retry, and profile-load reset paths? The
   persistent roster must clear for a new cup but survive race restarts within
   the current cup.
10. Are custom cups backed by the same `CupProfile` layout and same standings
    code as the four default cups?

## Implementation Checklist

Runtime:

- Add championship-aware support to `IsSupportedMode` or replace it with a
  target-count provider that handles Single Race and Championship separately.
- Add persistent cup roster state with clear lifecycle rules.
- Generate cup CPU models from `NumCars` and class counts.
- Reuse participant expansion/grid fixes for championship stages.
- Preserve the existing Clockwork Carnage post-race table behavior for any race
  with `participantCount > 16`.
- Add extra points/standings handling after Ghidra identifies the native code
  path.
- Add compact 30-car championship standings rendering if native UI is fixed to
  16 rows.

Generator/UI:

- Raise cup `numCars`, per-race required place, and overall required place caps
  from 16 to 30 where 30-car cups are enabled.
- Keep user-defined stage count at 16 unless a separate cup stage expansion is
  intentionally added. Stage count and car count are separate concerns.
- Update `DEFAULT_POINTS` and Rust `default_points_table` to 30 entries.
- Replace `pad_points` with a 30-entry pad/truncate helper for cups.
- Update `PointsTableEditor` to render 30 positions in a compact grid/table.
- Keep validation requiring `carsPerClass` sum to equal `numCars - 1`.
- Add validation tests for 16, 17, 24, and 30 cars.

QA:

- Single Race with 16, 17, 24, and 30 cars.
- Bronze/Silver/Gold/Platinum cups with 16, 17, 24, and 30 cars.
- Class distributions that need duplicate CPU models because too few unique
  CPU-selectable cars exist in a requested class.
- Race restart inside a cup.
- Failing a cup stage and retrying.
- Abandoning a cup and starting another cup.
- Finishing a cup with more than 16 cars and checking final standings/order.
- Loading a profile after a cup has been completed.

## Known Risks

- `CupProfile` should be treated as fixed-size native memory until proven
  otherwise. Extending the struct locally would corrupt adjacent fields.
- Existing 30-car state is reset per race. Championship roster persistence needs
  a separate lifetime.
- Native championship standings may index fixed 16-entry arrays even if
  `NumCars` is patched to 30.
- The current Clockwork Carnage result-table override is display-only. It does
  not solve cup points or standings storage.
- UI/generator support for 30-car cups should not be merged ahead of runtime
  support unless validation prevents generating unsupported configs.
